{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197631-now-how-long-can-a-nephandus-live","id":1197631,"title":"Now How long can a Nephandus live?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-20T09:05:06-07:00","id":1197631,"title":"Now How long can a Nephandus live?","content":"<span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>In Constantinople by night there is a Nephandus - Demon-mage LAYLA MADEER.</b></span></span></span> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The enigmatic owner of the House of Lamps is a mage who has lived beyond her years through loyal service to the Decani, an order of 36 demons of disease. Born in Alexandria, Layla was the wife of an Egyptian trader named Jiy\u2019al who brought grains to Constantinople for trade. Having made several allies within the city, Layla\u2019s husband moved to the capital to open shop as a grain merchant. He promised that he would send for his wife later.<br /> <br /> When Jiy\u2019al vanished and his brother sought to learn his fate, Layla managed to convince her brother-in-law to take her along. After several months in Constantinople, the two discovered that Jiy\u2019al had become a slave to his own vices and was now a thrall to people he called Setites. When Jiy\u2019al revealed his fate, Setites ambushed the three and the two brothers died. Layla\u2019s saving grace was the awakening of her Avatar, and the glowing corona of light that surrounded her. Though the display of power was minor, it was enough to send the frightened Setites scrambling and gave her the chance to escape into the night.<br /> <br /> Spending her next few days hidden, Layla eventually came upon the House of Lamps and felt a power beckoning from within. That\u2019s when she met Azzatti, a mage like herself and owner of the shop. He introduced her to her Awakened nature and to his dark masters. Ever since then, Layla has lived in the House of Lamps as a Nephandus \u2014 a demon-mage. <br /> <br /> When Azzatti died, Layla became owner of the shop and has defended it well. She is currently 140 years old and the fifth Nephandus to take ownership of the store. The House of Lamps is important because a Node lies beneath it \u2014 a source of power for magi \u2014 and the place is a Nephandus portal to the spirit realm.<br /> <br /> Layla has recently taken in the Baali known as Mary the Black, and is using her in an attempt to learn more about Cainites. Mary, however, is proving to be a powerful individual, and is enrapturing Layla with her own dark nature.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Now i am GM, and my players are going to play this campain from 365 ish and not from 1197. so i need to place this five nephandus in the time line i have constructed. </b></span></span><b>Now How long can a Nephandus live?</b></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23826-karrgoot","name":"Karrgoot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T09:12:44-07:00","id":1197637,"title":"","content":"As long as their dark masters deem it necessary and they can use Life effects to improve their health without getting 'doxed to death. Same as any mage, but with the added threat of getting eaten by a space squid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T09:38:59-07:00","id":1197647,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that unlike those corrupted by the Wyrm or 'fallen' to Oblivion, the Nephandi aren't inviting decay in. Not in that sense anyways. To my knowledge they can prolong their lives as long as any other Mage.<br /> <br /> It is also worth noting that old mages only leave the physical world behind because of the paradox that their long lives bring. Paradox (in the form of the Scourge) didn't really start manifesting until around the time of Sorcerer's Crusade (the 1400s), so I don't think there's any barrier to your Nephandus staying in Constantinople until it becomes Istanbul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T19:12:32-07:00","id":1197832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1197631-now-how-long-can-a-nephandus-live?p=1197647#post1197647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that unlike those corrupted by the Wyrm or 'fallen' to Oblivion, the Nephandi aren't inviting decay in. Not in that sense anyways. To my knowledge they can prolong their lives as long as any other Mage.<br /> <br /> It is also worth noting that old mages only leave the physical world behind because of the paradox that their long lives bring. Paradox (in the form of the Scourge) didn't really start manifesting until around the time of Sorcerer's Crusade (the 1400s), so I don't think there's any barrier to your Nephandus staying in Constantinople until it becomes Istanbul.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This.<br /> <br /> Technically, a sufficiently powerful Mage - Fallen or otherwise - could live for millennia, and spend a great deal of that time on Earth prior to the rise of the Scourge. The House of Lamps might have only ever had one owner before Layla, for all we know. Granted, this also requires that the Nephandus is powerful enough to prolong their life, AND be able to avoid death from any of the myriad ways they could die an unnatural death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T20:42:24-07:00","id":1197868,"title":"","content":"Since Nephandi are particularly unethical their options for prolonged life increase at the cost of the fact that more people want to kill you. Hell, pun intended, they could have made &quot;immortality&quot; one of their infernal investments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T12:48:17-07:00","id":1198076,"title":"","content":"Lo Pan from the <i>Book of Chantries</i> (and <i>Big Trouble in Little China</i>!) is a Nephandus that's been around since the 3rd century B.C., and there were supposed to be six Chou Yan of the Wu-Keng that were over 3,000 years old as of 1999. For that matter, Al-Aswad is still alive (or the functional equivalent) and he was the FIRST Nephandus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}